# s6 creates these inside each service directory at supervision time: the
# control fifo, the pid/status files, and the same again for the logger.
# Service definitions are symlinked into the scan directory rather than copied,
# which is what puts s6's runtime state inside the checkout.
#
# It is state, not configuration, so it is ignored rather than committed — see
# docs/LAYOUT.md. Do not "clean" these while the tree is running; s6 owns them.
supervise/
*/supervise/
